{{!--
  pages/privacy (ROUTES.md section 2, F-88, ADR 0016): the privacy notice. No guard and no session for guests.
  Model (pages.controller.ts): title. contactUrl comes from viewLocals (CONTACT_URL), so the contact channel is
  configuration, never a private address in markup (F-15, B-15). The imprint, when configured, is in the footer (F-89).
--}}
{{> page-heading title="Privacy" lead="What this site stores about you, who can see it and how to remove it."}}
<div class="long-text">
  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-operator">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-operator">who runs this site</h2>
    <p class="long-text__text">
      Nonsense Petition is a portfolio project run by Arnoldovna. For every question about your data, including
      requests to see or erase it, use the
      <a class="long-text__link" href="{{contactUrl}}">contact page of Arnoldovna</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-stored">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-stored">what is stored</h2>
    <ul class="long-text__list">
      <li class="long-text__item">your first and last name and your email address</li>
      <li class="long-text__item">a hash of your password, never the password itself</li>
      <li class="long-text__item">your age, city and homepage, only if you add them</li>
      <li class="long-text__item">your signature image and the time you signed</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="long-text__text">No IP addresses are stored in the database.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-visibility">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-visibility">who sees what</h2>
    <ul class="long-text__list">
      <li class="long-text__item">
        The supporters list shows your name, the date you signed and, if you added them, your age, city and homepage.
        Only registered users who are logged in can see it.
      </li>
      <li class="long-text__item">Your signature image is shown only to you.</li>
      <li class="long-text__item">Your email address is never shown to anyone else.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-purpose">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-purpose">why</h2>
    <p class="long-text__text">
      Your data is used to run this petition and for nothing else. There is no tracking, no analytics and no request
      to any third party. The site sets only the cookies it needs to work: one for your session and one that protects
      its forms against forgery. That is why there is no cookie banner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-retention">how long it is kept</h2>
    <ul class="long-text__list">
      <li class="long-text__item">Your account, profile and signature: until you delete them.</li>
      <li class="long-text__item">
        Your session: until you log out, after a period without activity, or at the latest after a fixed maximum
        lifetime, whichever comes first.
      </li>
      <li class="long-text__item">
        Counters that slow down repeated attempts, kept per network address range and per keyed hash of an email
        address: at most one hour.
      </li>
      <li class="long-text__item">Server logs: they name user ids only, never names or email addresses.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-deletion">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-deletion">deleting your data</h2>
    <ul class="long-text__list">
      <li class="long-text__item">
        To remove only your signature, <a class="long-text__link" href="/signature/delete">delete your signature</a>.
      </li>
      <li class="long-text__item">
        To remove your account, profile and signature together,
        <a class="long-text__link" href="/account/delete">delete your account</a>.
      </li>
      <li class="long-text__item">
        If you cannot log in any more, ask for erasure through the
        <a class="long-text__link" href="{{contactUrl}}">contact page</a>, writing from the email address of your
        account. Once that is confirmed, your account, profile and signature are erased together. You can ask for a
        copy of your data the same way.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="long-text__section" aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
    <h2 class="long-text__heading" id="privacy-rights">your rights</h2>
    <p class="long-text__text">
      You have the right to see the data stored about you, to correct it
      (<a class="long-text__link" href="/profile/edit">edit your profile</a>), to have it erased and to complain to a data
      protection supervisory authority.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
